    "body": "## Summary\n- add optional `category` slug filtering to public `GET /jobs`\n- support both precise leaf filtering and parent-category filtering across its selectable children\n- preserve the existing unfiltered repository/service path for backwards compatibility\n- add a hierarchical category/subcategory selector to the jobs page\n- validate category slugs at the API boundary and keep unknown valid slugs safely empty\n- document the public discovery contract and add focused service tests\n\n## Safety / privacy\n- discovery still exposes only public location labels; no exact coordinates or private labels are added\n- category filtering uses persisted server-side category relationships rather than trusting client display names\n- no Flyway migration is needed: the existing category catalog, unique slug, and job category FK already support this query\n\n## Verification\n- focused Mockito coverage for category normalization/routing and blank-category fallback\n- existing Maven tests and frontend lint/build remain the CI gate\n- do not merge until GitHub CI is green\n\n## Follow-up\nNearby/geospatial discovery can adopt the same category parameter in a separate small slice after this contract is proven, avoiding unnecessary coupling to the current on-site-location PR.",
